# Force LF line endings for everything git treats as text, regardless of
# which OS checks it out or commits it. This repo is developed from both a
# Linux environment and a Windows machine (zero's actual desktop, where the
# live apps - fitness/engine, learning/engine - run and write JSON state
# back into this repo). Without this, every JSON file those scripts save on
# Windows could get silently rewritten with CRLF line endings, making git
# see every single line as changed on the next diff/merge even when no
# value actually changed - see shared/libraries/json_store.py's save_json
# for the source-level half of this fix (newline="" on every JSON writer).
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries - never touch these no matter what.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.jfif binary
*.gif binary
*.glb binary
*.blend binary
*.stl binary
*.zip binary
*.7z binary
*.exe binary
*.msi binary
*.pdf binary
*.docx binary
*.xlsx binary
*.pptx binary
